{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1520740-misconceptions-about-2nd-edition","id":1520740,"title":"Misconceptions about 2nd Edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-15T20:45:57-07:00","id":1520740,"title":"Misconceptions about 2nd Edition.","content":"So I was browsing Spacebattles, and I found a guy spewing absolute vitriol re: Aberrant 2e. I\u2019ve copied several sections and highlighted the parts I felt were most relevant, and I want to get your take. Note: all bolding was done by me to emphasize the parts I deemed most relevant to his complaints, and all censorship was done by me. The original did not bother with asterisks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Aberrant War is physically impossible to stop in 2nd edition. Sure, they took away Mercer's paradox-proof time travel... but then <b>they changed Taint so that it is inevitable that any nova society eventually spirals down the Taint drain hole, the only question is 'how long'. As opposed to 1e's 'barring paradox proof time travel the tragedy was potentially avoidable, thus making it an actual tragedy that they didn't'.</b><br /> <br /> Even without a certain time traveling a**hole f***ing s**t up, even with Utopia 2e actually having sincere good intentions, they will still fail to integrate humanity and novas. <b>Because given enough time and die rolls, novas as a whole will inevitably go insane and have to be put down. They baked that straight into the physical laws of the universe.</b><br /> <br /> I really don't like Aberrant 2e for the outright d***slap it was to people who actually liked the idea of novas. They put a thicker shiny four-color veneer on top, and then f**ked with the foundations so that by the time you actually read deep enough to realize how f**ked you were... you'd already bought the book.<br /> <br /> F**k's sake, <b>going by the vanilla RAW it's impossible to so much as have novas use anything more than harsh language at each other without substantial property damage and a genuine risk of innocent deaths. The collateral damage table is at least as psychotically spiteful as the Taint rules. Even the Four-Color collateral rules (i.e., the optional ones that are less harsh than vanilla) still make novas as destructive as fanfic Glory Girl on a bad week, even when they're trying not to be.</b><br /> <br /> When I say that the game seems to want to spitefully punish its fanbase for daring to like novas I am not being sarcastic, I am saying that my sincere takeaway from having read the rules and the setting is that the writers genuinely seemed to hate that novas existed and damn sure don't like any player who actually wants to be one. Or to use a White Wolf analogy, it was like going from Hunters in oWoD to Heroes from the Beast: The Primordial in nWoD. </div> </div> </div><br /> Another bit from the same guy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you read the 2e Chrysalis rules? <b>Using them drives you as f**king insane as Taint does, you just take slightly longer and look a lot prettier doing it.</b><br /> <br /> Another thing I didn't like about 2nd edition was that <b>the flavor text straight-up lied to you at points about how the rules mechanics actually worked.</b> Not that this is unknown in White Wolf history, so Onyx Path is just continuing a proud tradition. </div> </div> </div>The guy did not provide any examples of this, sadly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People on Chrysalis 2e <b>have to take as many Transformations - what 1e called 'Aberrations' - as people not on Chrysalis do, they just get more freedom to pick which ones.</b> (This was actually a problem with Chrysalis 1e as well, but at least <b>Chrysalis 1e also gave you the option of losing temporary Taint before it became Permanent. To the best of my ability to determine, Chrysalis 2e closes out this possibility.</b>)<br /> <br /> Ergo, <b>staying on Chrysalis does not keep you from being Taint-buttered, it merely delays the process.</b> But soon enough you will run out of 'safer' Transformations to pick anyway - there's only a finite # - and at that point you're going full Divis Mal anyway. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> So, can anyone help me figure out some rebuttals to these points? It\u2019s quarter to midnight where I am, so I will be going to bed soon, but maybe sometime tomorrow morning you guys could help me out with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25249-deathbyflossing","name":"deathbyflossing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T01:10:58-07:00","id":1520749,"title":"","content":"While he's being rather extreme in his presentation, he's not wrong. Rules as written in <b>TC: Aberrant</b> <i>do</i> include a one-way ratchet where Transcendence only ever goes up, never down; and you <i>can't</i> achieve the power levels featured by Superman without losing your humanity: at the <i>very</i> least, you end up suffering massive social penalties that make being Clark Kent nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why I've got a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454210-avoiding-transcendence\">house rule</a> that grounding yourself can potentially reverse Transcendence: it doesn't have to be <i>easy</i> to lower Transcendence; but it <i>should</i> be <i>possible</i>. And as written, it isn't.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-16-2023, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T01:32:55-07:00","id":1520751,"title":"","content":"To be fair, though, while Transcendence only increases, the part about losing the ability to drain temporary Taint (flux) before it becomes permanent Taint (Transcendence) isn't true. You can reduce flux both with and without Chrysalis, though it's either slow or expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T03:09:02-07:00","id":1520754,"title":"","content":"The guy is not completely wrong in his suppositions, but he is starting from 3 points that I would avoid.<br /> <br /> The first point is Not all Novas are the PCs, and hardly any of them will change much their power levels at the speed the characters do. They will not Max Out that often, they will not botch (because they hardly roll), just because they are not exposed to the same level of stress as the character do. It results in Novas collecting less Flux all along, and resulting in an easier process of recovering without Chrysalis. Even the characters are usually not all time doing overwhelming things, the time off (in game terms, not only their time resting) usually is far less stressful and so less prone to flux.<br /> <br /> The second point is on power level. Novas are powerful, and a Q5 nova is capable of leveling a neighborhood with little effort and little time, they are not the \u201cusual novas\u201d if there is something like this, a Q5 nova can flood the entire coast of Fl\u00f3rida for example, with the proper powers, and by mistake. In 1e the general power level for the same Quantum dots is much lower, due to the nature of scale, for example, to destroy a planet with no effort the character needed Quantum 10 and a quantum power that was described in APG, basically to destroy planets, while in TC you need Q8 and quantum attack 8, it\u2019s enough to punch a planetary level punch, no maxing out.A Q6 nova can do the same by maxing out properly (3 successes). Most novas are in the Q1-3 level, capable of amazing deeds, according to their powers, but within the Comics level, from lifting airplanes and leveling houses, to run faster than any sport car, keeping the scale on proper levels.<br /> <br /> The last point is on duration of fights. A fight in TC last for 5-6 rounds, usually, less if one side is outnumbered, maybe a bit more with Novas, as they may have a lot of extra tools to prevent damage, but not that much more, so the Colateral dice will not be spent more than once in a fight, at least not in a common nova combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T07:12:47-07:00","id":1520767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can reduce flux both with and without Chrysalis, though it's either slow or expensive. </div> </div> </div>Is there a way to do so without dorming down? Because this guy did acknowledge that dorming down could do that, but he claimed you\u2019d have to spend entire game sessions dormed down in order to have any meaningful benefit, which he described as \u201cthe only safe way to play a nova is to not play <i>as</i> a nova\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25249-deathbyflossing","name":"deathbyflossing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T09:39:17-07:00","id":1520770,"title":"","content":"To be fair, check when was the date of publishing. When the bakers manuscript first show up, there were some different rules, particularly the rules for getting free of flux, making it really hard to lose flux. They changed before the backers PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"J